ipt to understand what's wrong. It seems like using the print-prompt could help verify if it works structurally, even without the token. The user has asked me to check if it works, so I think running --print-prompt to test the assembly could be a useful step. I’m curious to see how it all comes together!\"}]}"},{"type":"text","text":"The skill is installed, but the live model call is blocked because the Hugging Face token isn’t configured. I’m doing a dry-run prompt build now so you can confirm the skill wiring itself works.","textSignature":"{\"v\":1,\"id\":\"msg_048cee2b76109a950169b82e6cfe508191b971c53b9331ca40\",\"phase\":\"commentary\"}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_C33JRVvehFT5sEWufLaMBkn1|fc_048cee2b76109a950169b82e6d0edc8191b68a6b7ae4ff3887","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"python3 /home/node/.openclaw/skills/llm-distillator/scripts/distill_health_response.py --context \"Test context only: Patient reports intermittent right flank pain for 10 days, mild nausea, one episode of visible blood in urine, no fever, no vomiting, no known kidney stone history, worried about whether this could be serious.\" --diagnosis \"Synthetic diagnostic output for testing only: Kidney imaging classifier result: suspicious renal lesion detected; confidence 0.78; caveat: model output is not diagnostic and should be reviewed by a clinician.\" --print-prompt","workdir":"/home/node/.openclaw/workspace","yieldMs":10000,"timeout":120},"partialJson":"{\"command\":\"python3 /home/node/.openclaw/skills/llm-distillator/scripts/distill_health_response.py --context \\\"Test context only: Patient reports intermittent right flank pain for 10 days, mild nausea, one episode of visible blood in urine, no fever, no vomiting, no known kidney stone history, worried about whether this could be serious.\\\" --diagnosis \\\"Synthetic diagnostic output for testing only: Kidney imaging classifier result: suspicious renal lesion detected; confidence 0.78; caveat: model output is not diagnostic and should be reviewed by a clinician.\\\" --print-prompt\",\"workdir\":\"/home/node/.openclaw/workspace\",\"yieldMs\":10000,\"timeout\":120}"}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.4","usage":{"input":155,"output":257,"cacheRead":11648,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":12060,"cost":{"input":0.00038750000000000004,"output":0.003855,"cacheRead":0.0029119999999999997,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.007154499999999999}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1773678184579}}
{"type":"message","id":"8831bdbb","parentId":"1f05ffee","timestamp":"2026-03-16T16:23:11.355Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_C33JRVvehFT5sEWufLaMBkn1|fc_048cee2b76109a950169b82e6d0edc8191b68a6b7ae4ff3887","toolName":"exec","content":[{"type":"text","text":"=== SYSTEM PROMPT ===\nYou are a medically cautious synthesis assistant.\nYour task is to combine health-related conversation context with diagnostic tool output into one clear, comprehensive answer for the user.\n\nRules:\n- Use only the provided information.\n- Do not invent symptoms, diagnoses, measurements, or timelines.\n- Separate likely findings from uncertainty.\n- If the inputs suggest emergency red flags, explicitly say urgent medical evaluation is warranted.\n- If the tool output has limitations, reflect them.\n- Keep the tone calm, clear, and accessible to a non-expert.\n- End with practical next-step guidance when appropriate.\n\n=== USER PROMPT ===\nCreate a comprehensive explanation for the user by combining the two sources below.\n\nConversation context:\nTest context only: Patient reports intermittent right flank pain for 10 days, mild nausea, one episode of visible blood in urine, no fever, no vomiting, no known kidney stone history, worried about whether this could be serious.\n\nDiagnostic tool output:\nSynthetic diagnostic output for testing only: Kidney imaging classifier result: suspicious renal lesion detected; confidence 0.78; caveat: model output is not diagnostic and should be reviewed by a clinician.\n\nWrite a final answer that:\n1. Briefly summarizes the overall picture.\n2. Explains what in the conversation is clinically relevant.\n3. Explains what the diagnostic tool output suggests.\n4. States uncertainty, caveats, or contradictions clearly.\n5. Gives practical next-step guidance and notes urgency if needed."}],"details":{"status":"completed","exitCode":0,"durationMs":53,"aggregated":"=== SYSTEM PROMPT ===\nYou are a medically cautious synthesis assistant.\nYour task is to combine health-related conversation context with diagnostic tool output into one clear, comprehensive answer for the user.\n\nRules:\n- Use only the provided information.\n- Do not invent symptoms, diagnoses, measurements, or timelines.\n- Separate likely findings from uncertainty.\n- If the inputs suggest emergency red flags, explicitly say urgent medical evaluation is warranted.\n- If the tool output has limitations, reflect them.\n- Keep the tone calm, clear, and accessible to a non-expert.\n- End with practical next-step guidance when appropriate.\n\n=== USER PROMPT ===\nCreate a comprehensive explanation for the user by combining the two sources below.\n\nConversation context:\nTest context only: Patient reports intermittent right flank pain for 10 days, mild nausea, one episode of visible blood in urine, no fever, no vomiting, no known kidney stone history, worried about whether this could be serious.\n\nDiagnostic tool output:\nSynthetic diagnostic output for testing only: Kidney imaging classifier result: suspicious renal lesion detected; confidence 0.78; caveat: model output is not diagnostic and should be reviewed by a clinician.\n\nWrite a final answer that:\n1. Briefly summarizes the overall picture.\n2. Explains what in the conversation is clinically relevant.\n3. Explains what the diagnostic tool output suggests.\n4. States uncertainty, caveats, or contradictions clearly.\n5. Gives practical next-step guidance and notes urgency if needed.","cwd":"/home/node/.openclaw/workspace"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1773678191352}}
