{"type":"message","id":"e0ed1c0a","parentId":"3fbdbdff","timestamp":"2026-03-16T16:29:27.004Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"[[reply_to_current]] I checked the script and fixed the actual blocker.\n\nWhat was wrong:\n- The script had a real token hardcoded on line 17.\n- But the runtime check still treated that same value as a “placeholder,” so it always aborted before calling the API.\n\nWhat I changed:\n- Updated the token validation so it only fails when the token is actually empty.\n- Reran the synthetic test end-to-end.\n\nResult:\n- The skill now works and returned a full distilled patient-facing response from the model.\n\nSample live output themes:\n- It summarized the flank pain + hematuria context.\n- It explained the synthetic lesion detection result and its uncertainty.\n- It correctly preserved the caveat that the model output is not diagnostic.\n- It recommended urgent medical evaluation based on the made-up red-flag symptom.\n\nOne note:\n- There isn’t a git repo in the workspace right now, so there was nothing I could commit there.\n\nIf you want, I can also harden the script a bit more next — for example by removing the embedded token fallback entirely and relying only on environment variables, which would be safer.","textSignature":"{\"v\":1,\"id\":\"msg_048cee2b76109a950169b82fe1e9dc819182a2f4d2451945d4\",\"phase\":\"final_answer\"}"}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.4","usage":{"input":218,"output":232,"cacheRead":15104,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":15554,"cost":{"input":0.000545,"output":0.00348,"cacheRead":0.003776,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.007801}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1773678560938}}
